// Rite's published table says 3 means the source would not parse and 4 means it
// parsed but would not resolve. The binary did not do that: every rejection with
// an error in it exited 3 from `rite run`, and 4 from `rite check`, so the number
// told you which command had complained rather than what was wrong.
//
// This file is syntactically fine. `nowhere` is simply not defined (E020), which
// is a resolve failure and exits 4.
^ nowhere(1)
